Z||000016||tgowens||08-28-2000||10:20 PM||||well NDFieroTN -- as I mentioned earlier, there has been interest (at least two from each of the five states) to get it started -- also, as I mentioned earlier, I have no interest in running the club but am more than willing to help establish it (most of the work is already done, i.e. by-laws, web-site, etc...) I will also secure a domain name for the club and host the site with a per cost fee to come from the initial membership fees (not dues, but membership fees) -- there is a great need for a club of this type which will support Fiero owners from a broad area of the five states without requiring a lot of maintenance and intervention on anyones part (for example, there could be on-line meetings between responsible parties) -- <P>Now, as I mentioned earlier, I was not sure as to my plans for remaining in that area -- as it turns out, I came back to California last week (went through Memphis but it was 3:00 am and I thought better about getting in touch with you at that hour!!!) -- I am now, ans will be for a while, at the Fiero Shop (fieroshop on here) cranking out 3.4 upgrades  along with beginning a project on my blue '87 GT (making the blue one into a custom modified show car while leaving the gold GT primarily as a stock Fiero) -- I mention this in the event you or anyone back there needs parts -- feel free to email me at   <A HREF="mailto:terry@tgowens.com">terry@tgowens.com</A>   -- I am on George's computer right now and will not have mine set up again until after the move to the new shop in Richmond, CA next week -- I will be in touch again when I can get back online!!||||reg||1
